--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Generated code
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

There is none in this package, and that is a gap rather than a design choice.

Every other SDK's module surface is generated from the `loams.options.v1`
annotations on the protos by `protoc-gen-loams-facade`
(`crates/loams-facade-gen`). That crate ships renderers for TypeScript, Python,
Go and Rust. It ships no Swift renderer, so there is nothing that could generate a
Swift facade, and `scripts/sdk/gen.sh` accepts only
`typescript|typescript-live|python|go|rust`.

`Sources/Loams/Facade.swift`, `Sources/Loams/Reason.swift` and
`Sources/Loams/Messages.swift` are therefore NOT generated. They are the
hand-written Q604 fallback that design §44 §7.3 and D606 explicitly allow ("If the
plugin proves too costly for a language, that language falls back to a hand-written
facade checked by the same conformance suite"), and they carry the same
provenance note the Go SDK's facade does. When a Swift renderer lands they are
deleted and replaced with the same exported names.